        "original_id": "3ea0c766-8062-5da7-adc4-bf2c07ec2ef2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fetteresso Castle, Cowie Castle, Catterline, Cowie Water, Aberdeenshire, Scotland\n- Buildings: Fiddes Castle, Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, Muchalls Castle\n- Concepts: prehistoric use, Scottish gothic style, Palladian manor\n\nFacts:\n- Fetteresso Castle is a 14th-century towerhouse with clear evidence of prehistoric use of its site.\n- Fetteresso Castle was rebuilt in 1761 as a Scottish gothic style Palladian manor.\n- Cowie Castle is a ruined fortress in Aberdeenshire, Scotland.\n- The general area around Catterline includes Fetteresso Castle, Fiddes Castle, the Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, and Muchalls Castle as noted architectural or historic features.\n- Cowie Water is south of the ruined Cowie Castle.",
